#NEXUS

[ salgado2017a_fig4: Ornithischian time tree, read by eye. Three polytomies: the eight branches off the node above Pisanosaurus, Ornithopoda (three), and the ten-branch node holding Hypsilophodon to the Marginocephalia group; the node joining Talenkauen, (Parksosaurus, Gasparinisaura) and Iguanodontia is three-way. Ornithischia, Thyreophora, Neornithischia and Ornithopoda label nodes and are kept. The range bars and ovals are not branches. 29 tips, 4 polytomies (8, 3, 10, 3 children); 4 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 8 case (census 2, seed 20261251). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

